;; The version, in a file rather than in a BUILD attribute.
;;
;; clj_maven_export reads this in an ACTION, not during analysis. A bump re-runs the two
;; actions that read it — the pom generator, and the packaging step that puts the pom
;; inside the jar — and re-analyses nothing, where an attribute would make every release
;; a graph change. It is also the shape a Clojure project already has: the same file a
;; release workflow reads to check the tag, and a version-consistency test reads to
;; check the README.
;;
;; A bare "0.1.0" works too; the map is what most projects have.
{:version "0.1.0"}
